                        <decoDesc><decoNote>A crowned headpiece featuring a horizontal rectangular cartouche positioned directly above the main text block. The cartouche contains an anepigraphic field of solid gold, enclosed within a lapis lazuli blue fretwork border.                                
                                The crowned pediment above features a scalloped, dome-like ogival medallion filled predominantly with a gilt field of delicate arabesque and Khatā’ī floral motifs. At its center, it encloses a smaller ogival medallion with a deep indigo background, which in turn nests an inner ogival medallion in verdigris, both decorated with gold arabesque scrolling.                                
                                The main dome-like medallion also incorporates two green (verdigris) half-medallions at the outer edges and a small central medallion in saffron near the top. The area above the dome is skillfully filled with symmetrical floral sprigs on an unpainted ground. The entire headpiece is framed on three sides (moving outwardly) by a minium, a gilt, and a lapis lazuli blue panel, all executed with fine fretwork. 
                        </decoNote>
                            <decoNote> 
                                The text block is framed by triple-ruled border lines (black, thick gilt, and lapis lazuli blue, moving outwardly). Finally, the layout of the leaves is completed by a single black decorative frame that runs consistently along the outer margins of all subsequent pages.</decoNote>
                        </decoDesc>
                        <additions>
